# The kernel's wireless regulatory database. NOT part of linux-firmware — it is
# its own package, which is why every boot logged
#   cfg80211: failed to load regulatory.db
# and the live medium had no idea which country's channel and TX-power rules it
# was meant to obey. Cards that self-manage their regulatory domain in firmware
# (MediaTek's mt7921 among them) shrug this off; Intel, Atheros and Realtek parts
# fall back to the world-roaming domain, where much of 5 GHz is receive-only and
# TX power is capped at the most conservative value on earth.
wireless-regdb
# iw, because a live image is also a rescue image. Its absence is not cosmetic:
# with no `iw`, nothing on the medium can answer "what regulatory domain am I in"
# or "which channels does this radio actually have", which are the first two
# questions when wireless misbehaves. ~200 KB.
iw
openssh
sudo
seatd
systemd
mesa
